{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q412391","formula":"C₆H₁₀N₄","hill":"C6H10N4","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":10.0,"N":4.0},"names":{"en":"Pentetrazol","ru":"Пентилентетразол"},"descriptions":{"en":"Pentylenetetrazol (PTZ), or pentylenetetrazole, also known as pentetrazol (INNTooltip International Nonproprietary Name) and sold under the brand name Metrazol, is a drug formerly used as a circulatory and respiratory stimulant. High doses cause convulsions, as discovered by Hungarian-American neurologist and psychiatrist Ladislas J. Meduna in 1934. It has been used in convulsive therapy, and was found to be effective in treating depression, but side effects, such as uncontrolled seizures, were difficult to avoid.","ru":"Пентилентетразол (коразол, метразол) — лекарственное средство, ранее использовавшееся при острых отравлениях снотворными и некоторыми наркотиками (барбитуратами, бензодиазепинами, опиоидами)."},"fame":15,"pubchemCid":5917,"mass":138.17,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CCC2=NN=NN2CC1","inchikey":"CWRVKFFCRWGWCS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"6,7,8,9-tetrahydro-5H-tetrazolo[1,5-a]azepine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5917","atoms":20,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.567,"y":-0.641,"z":0.212,"el":"N"},{"x":1.783,"y":-1.105,"z":-0.111,"el":"N"},{"x":1.778,"y":1.123,"z":-0.134,"el":"N"},{"x":2.518,"y":-0.022,"z":-0.321,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.53,"y":-0.048,"z":-0.077,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.737,"y":-1.321,"z":-0.388,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.806,"y":1.261,"z":-0.402,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.524,"y":-1.532,"z":0.514,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.616,"y":1.56,"z":0.509,"el":"C"},{"x":0.567,"y":0.724,"z":0.198,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.839,"y":-0.051,"z":0.975,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.454,"y":-0.077,"z":-0.669,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.412,"y":-2.175,"z":-0.253,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.434,"y":-1.321,"z":-1.44